Fix GDMS calls hitting URLs that don't exist (v0.120)

v0.119 fixed the request-signing bugs, but every GDMS call still
failed - login with the generic Spring Security "Full authentication
is required to access this resource" 401, which is what you get when
a request doesn't match any real mapped endpoint at all. That pointed
at the URLs themselves rather than another signing problem.

Checking the doc's actual sample request URLs (rather than just its
short-form endpoint names in the parameter tables) turned up three
mistakes, all in how the request path is built:

1. The API version path segment is the literal string "1.0.0", not
   "v1.0.0" - baseUrl() had an extra "v" that doesn't belong.

2. Every Channel Management endpoint sits under a "/channel" prefix
   (the real path is "/channel/sub/list", not just "/sub/list") that
   GdmsChannelService wasn't adding at all.

3. "/oauth/token" (Getting Token and Refreshing Token) isn't under
   the versioned "/oapi/1.0.0" path at all - it's a bare "/oapi"
   endpoint. GdmsAuthService#login()/refresh() were building the
   token request under the same versioned baseUrl() as every other
   call, so login was never reaching a real endpoint - the most
   likely explanation for the "Full authentication is required"
   response, since that's Spring Security's default response for an
   unmapped route.

GdmsAuthService gains a private authBaseUrl() ("https://{domain}/oapi",
no version segment) used only by login()/refresh(); baseUrl() itself
just drops the stray "v". GdmsChannelService#post() now prefixes every
request path with "/channel".

gdms-api-findings.md (project doc) to be updated with this third fix
once it's confirmed working against BNS's real GDMS account.

